# pub reads this file INSTEAD of this directory's .gitignore, so it restates
# those rules below in addition to what it actually excludes.
#
# It also applies to SUBDIRECTORIES. That bit us once, back when this repo was a
# workspace: a `packages/` entry here also hid the members' own pubspecs, so
# `packages/sku_catalog_domain` failed validation with "The pubspec is hidden,
# probably by .gitignore or pubignore" while the root still reported 0 warnings.
# There are no sub-packages any more, so that particular trap is gone — but any
# rule added here reaches into every child directory, so keep them narrow and
# check `dart pub publish --dry-run`'s file list.

# Repo-only: agent instructions and the open-items list.
AGENTS.md
BACKLOG.md

# The whole test tree, not just what it imports. The reference backend is
# PUBLISHED (lib/in_memory.dart, lib/src/adapters/); what stays behind is the
# suite that tests it, which is repo-only — consumers are expected to build their
# own backend against the contracts. Readable on GitHub at
# github.com/taybiz/sku_catalog/tree/main/test.
test/

# From .gitignore
.dart_tool/
.packages
build/
pubspec.lock
doc/api/
.env*
*.dart.js
*.info.json
*.js
*.js_
*.js.deps
*.js.map
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# Written by `melos bootstrap`; pub reads THIS file, not .gitignore, so the
# exclusion has to be restated here for it to leave the published archive.
# (pub already drops dot-directories, but say it outright.)
*.iml
.idea/

# Written by `melos run coverage`. pub reads this file, not .gitignore, so a
# local coverage run would otherwise be published (pub tars untracked files).
coverage/
